JWT Lab (Node.js + Express)
A hands‑on, step‑by‑step lab to learn JSON Web Tokens (JWT) for authentication.
________________________________________
1) What & Why (2 minutes)
JWT = JSON Web Token used to prove identity between client and server. - Compact string with 3 parts: header.payload.signature (Base64URL-encoded) - Server issues token after login; client sends it in Authorization: Bearer <token> header for protected APIs.
Header: algorithm & type, e.g. { alg: "HS256", typ: "JWT" }
Payload: claims (user id, role, exp, iat)
Signature: HMACSHA256( base64url(header) + “.” + base64url(payload), secret )
________________________________________
2) Learning Outcomes
By the end, students can: - Explain the 3 parts of a JWT and typical claims (sub, iat, exp) - Implement login that returns a JWT with expiry - Protect routes using a verifyToken middleware - Test auth flow in Postman
