This installs 5 packages, each serving a specific purpose in JWT-based authentication.
Package	Purpose	Why it’s Needed in JWT Lab
express	Web framework for Node.js	To create our REST APIs like /login, /register, /profile
jsonwebtoken	Handles JWT creation and verification	Used for jwt.sign() (to generate tokens) and jwt.verify() (to validate tokens)
bcryptjs	For password hashing	We never store plain passwords — bcryptjs hashes them securely before saving
dotenv	Loads environment variables from .env file	We use .env to store secrets like JWT_SECRET, so we don’t hardcode them
cors	Enables Cross-Origin Resource Sharing	Allows frontend (like React app or Postman) to access our API from another origin



